    rationale:
      "Found by a research agent explicitly briefed on the full list of already-covered audit categories and the two immediately preceding iterations, and specifically asked to check whether sqlite-db-injectable-query-extraction's own self-described 'first step, not the full sweep' had a natural, low-risk continuation — it confirmed the 8 money/ledger and lead-pipeline race guards named in that PR's own follow-up note were still untested at the SQLite-query level, and that this is a genuine continuation of acknowledged-incomplete work, not a re-finding. Why it matters: SQLite is the fallback path every current deployment (this sandbox included) actually runs through when Convex is unconfigured, and every one of these functions is a guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE ... AND (<state still eligible>)` — a future refactor or merge-conflict resolution that silently drops one `AND` clause would leave tsc/lint/build/test all green while reintroducing exactly the double-payout, duplicate-receipt-email, or paid-lead-stage-revert bug each guard was written to prevent, since nothing beyond a manual dev-server check ever exercised the SQLite branch. Discovered mid-fix that the existing structural guard test (src/lib/db/lead-write-not-found-parity.test.ts, which statically greps db.ts's function source for the existence-check-then-throw pattern) would false-fail once updateLeadStage/recordLeadOutreach became one-line delegations to sqlite-queries.ts — fixed by adding resolveSqliteFallbackSource (lead-write-not-found-parity.ts) so the guard follows a `return sqlite<Name>(...)` delegation to the real function body in sqlite-queries.ts instead of checking db.ts's now-trivial pass-through, keeping the guard meaningful rather than papering over a false failure. Verified: 25 new Vitest cases (22 in sqlite-queries.test.ts covering all 7 extracted functions' happy-path and race-guard-rejection scenarios against real in-memory node:sqlite, 3 in lead-write-not-found-parity.test.ts covering resolveSqliteFallbackSource itself) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npm test (2484 passed = 2459 baseline + 25 new, 188 files) + a full clean rebuild (`rm -rf .next && npm run build`, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split) + npm run dev sanity check (deleted local.db, curled /dashboard/leads, /preview/example-bakery, /sitemap.xml — all 200, confirmed the seed log line with no errors, killed the dev server, deleted local.db afterward). This iteration's baseline checks (fresh npm ci, a fold-scan of the newest 11 remote branches by push time finding zero live candidates — all ahead=0 against origin/main except one already-confirmed-merged stale fork per session-fresh-clone-fold-scan-fetch-all-heads, mcp__github__list_pull_requests reconfirming the sole open PR is still #202, the same weeks-stale unrelated draft) all otherwise came back clean/unchanged and are not separately logged as their own entry. NEXT_STEPS unchanged (all five gated items stayed as-is) — this is a test-coverage/tech-debt fix, not a resolution of any gated item.",
